{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Did we not destroy their remnant?</b> — Most of the commentators said: it is קִמְנוּ with qamatz qatan, which is a ṣere under the mem. The correct view: it is without dagesh, and it is קָיַמְנוּ, and like it וְדִגְּגוֹ. If we did not destroy the blameless one mentioned above, we maintained him in the world, and the meaning is: we are witnesses that the blameless one did not die." "<b>Their surplus fire consumed</b> — the people of Sodom."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The verse lemma reads אם לא נכחד קימנו per the commentator's citation; the heading reflects this."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:27.617635956Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}